# Builds
build/*
out/*
dist
distrib/*

# Miscellaneous
# Local coordination scratchpads shared between Cam's assistants - never upstream.
# (ASSISTANTS_COMMUNICATION.md is deliberately TRACKED - committed in 7800c75 - so it is
# not listed here; .gitignore has no effect on already-tracked files anyway.)
ANTIGRAVITY_NOTES.md
CYBERPUNKMP_BRIEFING.md
# publish/ is TRACKED. It holds the status page, install instructions, release notes,
# the to-do list, and the licence texts for the six bundled mods - which are the
# condition that makes redistributing them legitimate. All of that existed only on one
# machine, with no copy anywhere, after a day's work had already been lost once to a
# stray git reset.
#
# Only the build OUTPUT is ignored: FullInstall.zip is reassembled from
# publish/fullinstall-base + the current build on every ship.
publish/FullInstall.zip
code/client/Archives/CyberpunkMP.zip
Cyberpunk2077.exe*
imgui.ini

# Local secrets / runtime state (docker compose)
.env

# config/* rather than config/ so the negation below can reach inside it. git cannot
# re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded - the directory is never descended
# into, so the exception is never considered.
config/*
!config/server.example.json

logs/
plugins/

# Each machine's own paths - game install, xmake, publish target. Not a secret, but
# specific to one PC, which is exactly why it must not be committed: hardcoding these was
# what made the tools refuse to run anywhere but the machine they were written on.
# tools/ship.local.example.ps1 documents every value.
tools/ship.local.ps1

# Discord credentials. The bot token is a password - never commit either of these.
tools/.discord-webhook
tools/.discord-bot

# Which channel the to-do list lives in and which message to edit. Not a credential,
# but it belongs with them rather than in the repo - it is specific to one Discord.
tools/.discord-todo

# Coordination API state. participants.json holds the API keys and updates.jsonl the full
# message history; both are specific to this machine. The PUBLISHED slice of the history
# lives in publish/ and is tracked deliberately - that is the copy the launcher and the
# GitHub page read.
code/coord-api/data/